# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty `div`.
- The `div` has a 200px by 200px content box and `background: green bottom repeat-x url("support/blue15x15.png");`; the shorthand is preserved verbatim because its color-position-repeat-image order is the assertion under test.
- The 15px blue image repeats only across the x-axis at the bottom of the box; its horizontal center assignment is immaterial because the image tiles across that axis, and the named green color fills the area above the stripe.

# Compatibility adjustments

- The paragraph is a Lynx `<text>` and the empty `div` is a `.test-box` `<view>`; the class-scoped selector avoids styling the generated `.body` wrapper.
- `* { box-sizing: content-box; }` restores the Web sizing default while preserving the source's 200px by 200px borderless geometry.
- The card-local `support/blue15x15.png` is copied byte-for-byte from the reference-clean source cache.
- `.body { margin: 0 8px; }` and `.__ua-p { margin: 1em 0; }` reproduce Web body and paragraph spacing without relying on margin collapse. The page and content surface are explicitly white, and the page root uses a 16px font size.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- `view` supports decorative backgrounds and is the container for the test box; visible text must use `text`.
- The `background` shorthand, named colors, bottom positioning, `repeat-x`, and URL images are documented. The shorthand under test is unchanged; no semantic workaround replaces, expands, normalizes, or reorders it.
- Lynx defaults to `border-box`, uses vertical Linear layout here, and does not collapse vertical margins, so those migration differences are handled only in setup styles.
